{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation","id":1054739,"title":"How do Proud Warriors respond to Humiliation?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-25T07:09:59-08:00","id":1054739,"title":"How do Proud Warriors respond to Humiliation?","content":"So hypothetically, a Methesulah wakes up and tries to reclaim some site of importance to him, which is a sacred place to &quot;the lupines&quot;, not that they care obviously. They use some combination of Presence, Dominate, Obfuscate and Blood Magic (Obfuscate to sneak in, Blood Magic to confound spiritual defenses, Presence and Dominate to get them all to leave/run) to cast out the Garou (we're coming into this assuming that some Elders have that power, that's a prerequisite to the hypothetical. I really don't want to get into an &quot;8 Werewolves in Crinos vs. Mithras&quot; situation, how strong a group of NPCs and one NPC are is a plot device).<br /> <br /> How would a group of Garou and Kinfolk respond to being kicked out of their Caern? We're assuming that something is stopping them from just attacking the Elder during the day (Ward Against Lupines isn't too hard to pull off, most Methesulah's have Dominate, Presence or some form of Blood Magic to do it themselves, and Ward Against Spirits isn't out of the question either).<br /> <br /> Right now I'm imagining them going into a frenzy (not Frenzy) and gathering up all of the Tribes and Packs they can find, all the spirits who will support them, tearing down the Ward and destroying the Elder in the middle of the day. What obstacles would they face? Stereotypically, would other Werewolves (I'm assuming this will vary by tribe, auspice and whatnot) be on board with helping them reclaim it, or would they look down upon them (they've been kicked out of their home and they approach with their tale between their legs).<br /> <br /> Is it a case of politics, pride and overcoming tribal fractures? This isn't too far off the Apocalypse/Gehenna, we're past 2000 and so would different Packs and Tribes ignore old quarrels to reclaim the site? Would they demand some sort of price, or would that be considered abhorrent?<br /> <br /> Assuming that Ratkin and Ananasi are hiding in the shadows, how would they feel about such events?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 02-25-2017, 10:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T07:33:13-08:00","id":1054744,"title":"","content":"From a Garou game point of view:<br /> <br /> Losing a Caern is a tragedy to the Garou. Yet, Caerns have fallen before to the Black Spiral Dancers or have been depleted by mages. Losing to a Vampire may sting a bit more, but what can you do in these dark days?<br /> <br /> There will be consequences to the fall of the caern. First, it will be a renown hit to the survivors. They fucked up and lost a sacred site to Gaia. Losing a Caern may make higher status Garou perform the Rite of the Winter Wolf (ritual suicide). Younger Garou will have that follow their reputation for the rest of their lives. While the survivors will probably want to gather Garou from other septs and ride in to take the caern back, the tribal elders will disagree. They would want the survivors to go to another caern and make sure no other caerns fall. They are thinking about the good of the whole Garou nation. You can't let the reclamation of one Caern leave the other caern's defenseless. Note, if this is a Level 5 Caern, the elders may be tempted to take it back, only because most likely it was their HOME that was lost. <br /> <br /> From a Vampire game point of view:<br /> <br /> Those fuzzy bastards are going to keep coming back until they get their home back. The Lupine may be a useful tool for getting rid of some annoying rivals. <br /> <br /> <br /> Though to be honest, most caerns are in places that Vampires don't go. They are located in Wilderness with few people to feed on. An urban caern would be more tempting, but the Bone Gnawers and Glasswalkers would expect and be prepared for Vampire attacks. Though perhaps not from a low generation vampire. As a vampire PC, I'd be more worried as to why an elder vampire wants a Lupine holy site. It's a place of power, so what nefarious plans do they have for all that supernatural energy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T07:37:49-08:00","id":1054745,"title":"","content":"They would be mostly dead, I'd say. Litany forbids letting a Caern be damaged, and Vampires are big enough eff you to garou that they would fight to the last garou. Those who escape might try to drum up interest, and a war party might help. But in general a bunch of vampires with no bane or BSD allies coming to claim a Caern either gets wiped out fast, or the fight will destroy the whole area.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Or, what wonderandawe said, mostly just the garou scattering to the winds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","user":"Ana Mizuki","date":". 02-25-2017, 10:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T08:23:06-08:00","id":1054756,"title":"","content":"So the chances of a whole Caern's Garou just walking off....because? Not likely. A good majority of the population should be dead from fighting to defend the Caern. From the survivors, that's mostly been covered (going to other Septs and or the Rite of the Winter Wolf are likely possibilities), but I will add an additional thought on the idea of taking back the Caern.<br /> <br /> I do think there is a good chance of survivors trying to rally enough forces to take back the Caern though (&quot;trying&quot; being the key word there). Whether or not that is realistic will depend entirely on the amount of allies the individuals left have ties to. And the higher the Caern level the more likely you can pull in help. However...even if you take the Caern back, there is a good chance you don't get to keep it. The help you brought in has completely legitimate reasons to claim the Caern themselves afterwards. So that's a factor to consider. Personally, even if someone else claimed the Caern, I think it would be worth it to have it back in Gaian hands.<br /> <br /> On the last bit thrown in there:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation#post1054739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Assuming that Ratkin and Ananasi are hiding in the shadows, how would they feel about such events?</div> </div> </div> </div>Neither of them care. Not even a little bit unless it is going to directly impact them. The Ratkin might have a quick chuckle and go on about their day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 02-25-2017, 11:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T08:38:17-08:00","id":1054766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1054756#post1054756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the chances of a whole Caern's Garou just walking off....because? Not likely.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the implication is that Dominate and Presence are used on them to tell them to go away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T08:44:19-08:00","id":1054768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1054766#post1054766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the implication is that Dominate and Presence are used on them to tell them to go away.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly, and we're talking Level 8 or 9 powers so it's becoming more and more reasonable as an outcome. The issue is Frenzy, which is why Obfuscate is desirable. Even Ventru would have difficulty dealing with a group of Lupines who are in total Frenzy, since it makes dealing with Dominate and Presence very easy (unless the ST decides that Dominate 10 even effects animalistic minds, but that would be a bit... theme-breaking).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T08:46:15-08:00","id":1054770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1054756#post1054756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the chances of a whole Caern's Garou just walking off....because? Not likely. A good majority of the population should be dead from fighting to defend the Caern. From the survivors, that's mostly been covered (going to other Septs and or the Rite of the Winter Wolf are likely possibilities), but I will add an additional thought on the idea of taking back the Caern.<br /> <br /> I do think there is a good chance of survivors trying to rally enough forces to take back the Caern though (&quot;trying&quot; being the key word there). Whether or not that is realistic will depend entirely on the amount of allies the individuals left have ties to. And the higher the Caern level the more likely you can pull in help. However...even if you take the Caern back, there is a good chance you don't get to keep it. The help you brought in has completely legitimate reasons to claim the Caern themselves afterwards. So that's a factor to consider. Personally, even if someone else claimed the Caern, I think it would be worth it to have it back in Gaian hands.<br /> <br /> On the last bit thrown in there:<br /> <br /> Neither of them care. Not even a little bit unless it is going to directly impact them. The Ratkin might have a quick chuckle and go on about their day.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking about them losing the Caern to those who help them recover it. Makes sense.<br /> <br /> Surely the Ananasi COULD care, hypothetically? A powerful Vampire taking control of a site of mystical power is potentially quite a big deal. However they're just as likely to say &quot;oh, yes, all part of our grand plan&quot; as they are to do anything about it, am I right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T08:47:51-08:00","id":1054771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1054768#post1054768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Exactly, and we're talking Level 8 or 9 powers so it's becoming more and more reasonable as an outcome. The issue is Frenzy, which is why Obfuscate is desirable. Even Ventru would have difficulty dealing with a group of Lupines who are in total Frenzy, since it makes dealing with Dominate and Presence very easy (unless the ST decides that Dominate 10 even effects animalistic minds, but that would be a bit... theme-breaking).</div> </div> </div> </div>I should note that garou can resist vampire powers with Rage, and given vampires are attacking them, I'd say there is a bit of it to go around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T08:54:16-08:00","id":1054774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1054744#post1054744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though to be honest, most caerns are in places that Vampires don't go. They are located in Wilderness with few people to feed on. An urban caern would be more tempting, but the Bone Gnawers and Glasswalkers would expect and be prepared for Vampire attacks. Though perhaps not from a low generation vampire. As a vampire PC, I'd be more worried as to why an elder vampire wants a Lupine holy site. It's a place of power, so what nefarious plans do they have for all that supernatural energy?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well in this case it's kind of coincidental. Before he fell into Torpor a battle took place there, and someone he cared deeply for was destroyed there. He's literally just gone there to mourn for a few months while controlling things from afar, before retreating somewhere more safe. Since he's a potent blood mage he might make use of the ambient energy there, but for a Blood Mage a Caern is like giving a nuclear reactor to someone and saying &quot;here's some energy&quot;, I doubt he could harness it and even if he could it wouldn't have the best results.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T08:57:17-08:00","id":1054775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1054771#post1054771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I should note that garou can resist vampire powers with Rage, and given vampires are attacking them, I'd say there is a bit of it to go around.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well... look at it this way. Willpower 10 and the Iron Will merit make you practically immune to Dominate. But Iron Will does nothing to Elder Level Dominate powers (well, kind of, but brushing over it very quickly that's the gist). I'd doubt the ability of Rage to counter Level 8 Dominate from someone with a ridiculous dice-pool... but this is exactly the discussion I was trying to avoid, brushing over things, we'll say if a Vampire's Power Level is over 9000 then they can Dominate Garou with a high success rate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T09:00:21-08:00","id":1054777,"title":"","content":"I feel like this whole hypothetical is predicated on a vampire with nearly god-tier powers; if you have a methuselah walking around in your game with dominate 8-9 and the one specific obscure Thaumaturgy path that deals with umbral spirits, anything goes. You are just making stuff up at that point, rules hardly matter and precedent isn't really set. This is like asking what happens to the local vampire court if an elder Theurge convinced an avatar of Helios manifest in Elysium. They get fucked, most of them die, and the survivors, if there are any, are in a bad way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T09:12:34-08:00","id":1054783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1054777#post1054777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like this whole hypothetical is predicated on a vampire with nearly god-tier powers; if you have a methuselah walking around in your game with dominate 8-9 and the one specific obscure Thaumaturgy path that deals with umbral spirits, anything goes. You are just making stuff up at that point, rules hardly matter and precedent isn't really set. This is like asking what happens to the local vampire court if an elder Theurge convinced an avatar of Helios manifest in Elysium. They get fucked, most of them die, and the survivors, if there are any, are in a bad way.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Ignoring all but a bit of this since it's thread-capping, generally quite negative and provokes the question &quot;why comment then?&quot; more than anything else (whilst oddly also questioning the value of hypothetical questions entirely)...</i><br /> <br /> RE Spirit Thaumaturgy, Ward Against Spirits is a generic level 5 Thaumaturgy Ritual which affects intangible beings. &quot;Stay away spirits&quot; isn't too hard to pull off, even with relatively common Blood Magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T09:14:02-08:00","id":1054784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1054756#post1054756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However...even if you take the Caern back, there is a good chance you don't get to keep it. The help you brought in has completely legitimate reasons to claim the Caern themselves afterwards. So that's a factor to consider.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was my thought, too. If they could muster the power to take back the Caern, said power would likely not leave them in charge for their failure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1054770#post1054770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Surely the Ananasi COULD care, hypothetically? A powerful Vampire taking control of a site of mystical power is potentially quite a big deal. However they're just as likely to say &quot;oh, yes, all part of our grand plan&quot; as they are to do anything about it, am I right?</div> </div> </div> </div>That drastically depends on what's at stake for the Ananasi. If it's just some random Caern, she's liable to not care too much. It's not her business, her fight, or her problem. Ananasi tend to have two main, driving goals: 1) Free mommy from the Wyrm, and 2) Restore the balance of the Triat. Also keep in mind that there are werespiders who specifically &quot;work for&quot; each of the members of the Triat, in their efforts to restore balance (ultimately, they work for Ananasa, but they actively aid the soothing of the Triat). This will color their perception on how things should play out.<br /> <br /> They have smaller goals as they go throughout their business, but these goals will likely ultimately tie back into those big two. If one of the people (on either side) involved in the battle is someone that she needs for whatever reason or another, and she can leverage this into a position of personal gain (say, a huge favor in return), then maybe she'd care. But think in a calculating way. It's ridiculously risky for an Ananasi to get involved in this kind of ordeal. If that particular Caern means something in the greater scheme of things (perhaps some prophecy or something similar), she might try to influence which direction things go in (obviously to whichever direction serves her needs).<br /> <br /> So, in short, would the random Ananasi give a damn? Probably not. If you're the ST, you'd have to provide a plausible motivation for why she'd care at all. It'd likely have to connect to her big goals somehow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12777,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12777-wakuwa","user":"Wakuwa","date":". 02-25-2017, 12:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12777-wakuwa","name":"Wakuwa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12777_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T09:17:08-08:00","id":1054785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1054777#post1054777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like this whole hypothetical is predicated on a vampire with nearly god-tier powers; if you have a methuselah walking around in your game with dominate 8-9 and the one specific obscure Thaumaturgy path that deals with umbral spirits, anything goes. You are just making stuff up at that point, rules hardly matter and precedent isn't really set. This is like asking what happens to the local vampire court if an elder Theurge convinced an avatar of Helios manifest in Elysium. They get fucked, most of them die, and the survivors, if there are any, are in a bad way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it is an atom bomb. They can build from it, sure. But most likely it is just a lot of dead garou.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T09:30:06-08:00","id":1054795,"title":"","content":"I was kind of annoyed since it seemed a little too perfect of a Kobayashi-Maru scenario for the werewolves, but you are discussing this in good faith, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11620_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11620\" data-vbnamecard=\"11620\">twig</a>. I should not have come off so harshly.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1054783#post1054783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">RE Spirit Thaumaturgy, Ward Against Spirits is a generic level 5 Thaumaturgy Ritual which affects intangible beings. &quot;Stay away spirits&quot; isn't too hard to pull off, even with relatively common Blood Magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh. That is how it is doing it? That is more common, sure, but it is also comparatively weak. The ritual states that it works exactly like Ward Against Ghouls, but that only effects one object, and even then, only hurts the spirit if it comes in direct contact. You arguably could not ward a 'whole caern' since it gives the example of specific car parts being warded, rather than the car holisitically (although as I re-read the original ghoul-warding ritual, it now it seems like spirit-killing bullets are on the table. Impractical, given the existence of the Gauntlet, but awesome nonetheless).<br /> <br /> That vamp is gonna have a rough time, because charms can still effect it, and if the spirits know incite frenzy, they very well could use it on their own packs in order to goad them into defending a caern when they would otherwise flee. Edit: and even if the spirits were in direct contact with the ward via manifestation or other shenanigans, they would likely just grit their teeth/teeth analogues and take the damage, since most spirits of relevant caliber have a fairly large pool of essence. They are fighting for their home too, and totem spirits have as much, if not more, invested in the caern than the Garou do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 02-25-2017, 12:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T09:40:14-08:00","id":1054806,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3695_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3695\" data-vbnamecard=\"3695\">The Laughing Stranger</a> All of the Warding Object rituals have a Warding Area equivalent which can be fast-cast. While I haven't storytold every second of it, I imagined him Warding his own body and then constructing a large Area Ward using Warded objects as ritual tools (can't have them throwing stuff about while he's not looking). He has a lot of blood to work with and he's surrounded by potential ritual ingredients. After two night's work he could quite reasonably have the entire Caern Warded against Spirits and Lupines (not kinfolk), and have a host of Vampires and Ghouls defending him. I didn't want to get into practicalities, but since it's pertinent to their political response it seems good to clarify.<br /> <br /> And thanks for apologizing. I often find that on every Forum here, if someone posts something a bit off the wall one of the first responses is typically &quot;this post shouldn't have happened&quot;, and it's something that bothers me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T10:00:12-08:00","id":1054817,"title":"","content":"I guess I am fuzzy on the chronology. The vamp wards itself, stealths into the caern via obfuscate, and then reveals itself while commanding any Garou within earshot to leave? Even if it is warded, can't spirits just... see the dead thing coming? A vamp that old is almost certainly of the Wyrm, and that is why you have sentries in the first place. Assuming the Garou go and attack, sure, it can still just tell them all to go fuck themselves, but again, it currently only has wards on one thing, itself; what if the the spirits incite the Garou to frenzy or just attack using blast charms or updrafts, curses, or whatever else they have going on? Where is the Methuselah finding the time to keep the spirits off of its back with just that one ritual? I am not sure that is anywhere near enough to circumvent the spiritual defenses of the caern.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T10:18:49-08:00","id":1054827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1054817#post1054817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess I am fuzzy on the chronology. The vamp wards itself, stealths into the caern via obfuscate, and then reveals itself while commanding any Garou within earshot to leave? Even if it is warded, can't spirits just... see the dead thing coming? A vamp that old is almost certainly of the Wyrm, and that is why you have sentries in the first place. Assuming the Garou go and attack, sure, it can still just tell them all to go fuck themselves, but again, it currently only has wards on one thing, itself; what if the the spirits incite the Garou to frenzy or just attack using blast charms or updrafts, curses, or whatever else they have going on? Where is the Methuselah finding the time to keep the spirits off of its back with just that one ritual? I am not sure that is anywhere near enough to circumvent the spiritual defenses of the caern.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the omniscience of spirits can scupper just about anything. My answer would be that in order to balance Werewolves, I've said that the Spirits of the Umbra need to be actively scanning with Sense Wyrm and the like, they don't have innate alarm bells. When you have Werewolves in the same city as Vampires, you don't need to give the Lupines invisible sentries. I wouldn't do that in a Werewolf game. Basically I'm using Werewolves as they exist in WTA, but the power levels are modified to make the Players feel like they might have some distant chance of fooling the Werewolves or escaping them if there was a confrontation. Subtle under-dog powers are for tricksy Sorcerers and Ghosts, whereas the Werewolves at my Vampire table are Physical Beasts who can call on spirits in times of great need, and have awesome tricks which are more showy than subtle. So your Werewolf can fight like a Gangrel Elder, create a burst of flames, drive pheremones up to 11 in humans, heal really fast, move like the wind across the city... that sort of thing. RE Frenzy, Presence 2 with a huge dicepool and a lot of difficulty modifications (some merits to do with his gaze, plus the specializations which come from having Intimidate at 7) can leave enemies with a dicepool of 0 and force them to run away, Frenzy or otherwise. That's the humiliating aspect; &quot;the damn leech just looked at me. I... I've never felt more scared in my life. It was like I was powerless, and reason and courage and duty just fell away...&quot;. Defeat by physical means might have some more honour. They'd die or bear physical injuries. Being forced to run away by Wyrmish powers of cowardice alone is true humiliation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 02-25-2017, 01:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T10:26:59-08:00","id":1054831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1054817#post1054817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess I am fuzzy on the chronology. The vamp wards itself, stealths into the caern via obfuscate, and then reveals itself while commanding any Garou within earshot to leave? Even if it is warded, can't spirits just... see the dead thing coming? A vamp that old is almost certainly of the Wyrm, and that is why you have sentries in the first place. Assuming the Garou go and attack, sure, it can still just tell them all to go fuck themselves, but again, it currently only has wards on one thing, itself; what if the the spirits incite the Garou to frenzy or just attack using blast charms or updrafts, curses, or whatever else they have going on? Where is the Methuselah finding the time to keep the spirits off of its back with just that one ritual? I am not sure that is anywhere near enough to circumvent the spiritual defenses of the caern.</div> </div> </div> </div>So I 100% agree on the points of why this shouldn't happen or why it is a hell of a lot more difficult than presented. But I'm doing my best to gloss over it since that was part of the premise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1054766#post1054766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I think the implication is that Dominate and Presence are used on them to tell them to go away.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1054768#post1054768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Exactly, and we're talking Level 8 or 9 powers so it's becoming more and more reasonable as an outcome. The issue is Frenzy, which is why Obfuscate is desirable. Even Ventru would have difficulty dealing with a group of Lupines who are in total Frenzy, since it makes dealing with Dominate and Presence very easy (unless the ST decides that Dominate 10 even effects animalistic minds, but that would be a bit... theme-breaking).</div> </div> </div> </div>Since Dominate generally takes 5 successes to get someone to act directly against their Nature (and even then it isn't 100%) I find it hard to believe this happens without a fight. I am 100% willing to concede the premise that Methuselah walks in and takes a Caern. This cannot and will not happen without Garou casualties though. So the scenario (for me) then plays out as: what do the survivors do now? I suppose I can just walk away from the thread if that compromise isn't enough for me to then comment on the follow up reactions of survivors.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1054783#post1054783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <i>Ignoring all but a bit of this since it's thread-capping, generally quite negative and provokes the question &quot;why comment then?&quot; more than anything else (whilst oddly also questioning the value of hypothetical questions entirely)...</i><br /> <br /> RE Spirit Thaumaturgy, Ward Against Spirits is a generic level 5 Thaumaturgy Ritual which affects intangible beings. &quot;Stay away spirits&quot; isn't too hard to pull off, even with relatively common Blood Magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ward vs Spirits cannot ward against the Caern Spirit. It is metaphysically anchored to the Caern/land. So that Spirit will have to be killed or beaten into slumber or unbound from the area. None of those tasks are easy. And none of them are going to happen while the Garou walk off because of Presence or Dominate. Also, Obfuscate isn't going to work against the Caern Spirit or most of the Caern's non-Garou defenders. All of this though was supposed to be taken as given facts within the premise, so I am trying not to pick at them too much.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 02-25-2017, 01:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T10:28:39-08:00","id":1054834,"title":"","content":"I think a big issue here is spirits are kind of irritatingly effective against things with no reliable way to deal with them. In a werewolf game, spiritual enemies are a primary threat, so spirits being constantly vigilant is kind of necessary. Spirit-stuff is kind of a blind spot for vampires, though, which is fine since that isn't really a theme that fits terribly well with the vampiric mindset/worldview. If you want to tone down spirits to level the playing field for a vampire game, I totally get that. It can actually make werewolves pretty unfun to play against as a vampire, sort of like how it can feel kind of hopeless if you pit a werewolf against a potent and prepared mage antagonist.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 02-25-2017, 01:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T10:32:24-08:00","id":1054840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1054834#post1054834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a big issue here is spirits are kind of irritatingly effective against things with no reliable way to deal with them. In a werewolf game, spiritual enemies are a primary threat, so spirits being constantly vigilant is kind of necessary. Spirit-stuff is kind of a blind spot for vampires, though, which is fine since that isn't really a theme that fits terribly well with the vampiric mindset/worldview. If you want to tone down that to level the playing field for a vampire game, I totally get that. It can actually make werewolves pretty unfun to play against as a vampire, sort of like how it can feel kind of hopeless if you pit a werewolf against a potent and prepared mage antagonist.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get that. A Mage with Spirit 3 or higher makes your best friends who you've bonded to for years into his puppets with ease. It feels... unfair. Thankfully he's squishy and far from invincible, you just need to outsmart him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T10:34:22-08:00","id":1054843,"title":"","content":"Does the Caern spirit need beating, though? Or, CAN the vampires do it? What if the spirit remains there, sniping at the vampires spiritually while they are none the wiser?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T10:36:29-08:00","id":1054844,"title":"","content":"Just to close the book on all of this, Far Mastery and Auspex 5/6 are all he needs to Dominate them all into leaving from a good distance away. It just costs 2 points of Willpower, and can easily be combined with Group Dominate which is level 7 I believe. I don't want to have a pissing match, this isn't the point of this thread, it's supposed to be un fait accompli, but I'd like to settle the mechanical matter. And at the end of the day it's all plot devices.<br /> <br /> The real question is why he hasn't Dominated the PCs to walk outside in the middle of the day, but it's 2 Willpower a pop and recovering Willpower is tricky when you're emotionally isolated and mourning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T10:37:37-08:00","id":1054846,"title":"","content":"Re-reading the last few posts, I am not sure if the 'werewolf spirit nerf' is because your PCs need to have counterplay, or because otherwise the Methuselah would have too difficult of a time taking over the caern.<br /> <br /> Having a crossover with werewolves is fine, but why even bother making them seem like WtA Garou? Why not just make them lupines, which are still dangerous, obviously, but vampires then don't have to deal with all the weird spirit magic (which you would be nerfing anyway; might as well jettison it for simplicity's sake). Also, if you need to nerf the Garou so that your players can more easily interact with them, that is fine. If you need to weaken them in order for your crazy McGuffin vampire to beat them, that is fine too, but you don't need our input at that point, since we are talking less about how werewolves as WtA players would run them, and more like the watered-down lupines of VtM (which, again, is fine, but this discrepancy might explain why you are getting a fair amount of pushback on the specifics of this scenario).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T10:37:43-08:00","id":1054847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1054843#post1054843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the Caern spirit need beating, though? Or, CAN the vampires do it? What if the spirit remains there, sniping at the vampires spiritually while they are none the wiser?</div> </div> </div> </div>A Master Thaumaturge could slowly corrupt the spirit and twist it to a new purpose. A group with Spirit Thaumaturgy could pull it off. Alternatively, I'm musing on some BSDs or Wyrm-tainted Mages/Sorcerers offering to assist him in exchange for access to the shrine (calling him their Prince, showing respect etc.).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T10:39:15-08:00","id":1054849,"title":"","content":"So the most obvious vampire I can think of that fits these Discipline requirement are Setites (Obfuscate, Presence and Blood Magic). And if this scenario was a real possibility, then the Setites would have just wandered into Strider Caerns and politely (Presence) asked them to leave. Since we know their conflicts were a lot more in depth than that, I have to conclude that the base scenario just doesn't really work. And that's without going in depth on the spirit matters or specific resistances.<br /> <br /> Now, if you accept that Garou will have to die to make this work, then you can see it really is a dangerous situation for the Vampire involved which then goes a long way to explain why this doesn't just happen all the time.<br /> <br /> And neither of those conceits alter to core question of what the Garou then do after their Caern has been taken. War parties are a distinct possibility, supported by spirits and Fetishes, because that's how the Garou work. Ward vs Lupines and Spirits are remarkably weak and only really work as written in pure Vampire games because the STs say they do. The newer versions written at least have a non damage portion of the ritual that makes it more difficult. Older versions just did pathetic damage as a deterrent. But even still, those Wards can be broken. And I'm curious what the mechanic for fast casting them is that you mentioned. I was under the impression that Thaum Rituals were very much actual magic Rituals you had to set up and spend real time putting in place.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T10:39:17-08:00","id":1054850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1054846#post1054846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having a crossover with werewolves is fine, but why even bother making them seem like WtA Garou? Why not just make them lupines, which are still dangerous, obviously, but vampires then don't have to deal with all the weird spirit magic (which you would be nerfing anyway; might as well jettison it for simplicity's sake). Also, if you need to nerf the Garou so that your players can more easily interact with them, that is fine. If you need to weaken them in order for your crazy McGuffin vampire to beat them, that is fine too, but you don't need our input at that point, since we are talking less about how werewolves as WtA players would run them, and more like the watered-down lupines of VtM (which, again, is fine, but this discrepancy might explain why you are getting a fair amount of pushback on the specifics of this scenario).</div> </div> </div> </div>I've posted here because while I'm watering down the mechanical powers of Werewolves, I'm keeping the relevant lore. For example these are Red Talons and they've been warring with some other Garou in the surrounding area over a grudge to do with them killing some human kinfolk (fault on both sides). That's WTA. WTA doesn't stop being WTA when you remove subtle gifts and weaken the omniscience of spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T10:43:39-08:00","id":1054852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1054849#post1054849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the most obvious vampire I can think of that fits these Discipline requirement are Setites (Obfuscate, Presence and Blood Magic). And if this scenario was a real possibility, then the Setites would have just wandered into Strider Caerns and politely (Presence) asked them to leave. Since we know their conflicts were a lot more in depth than that, I have to conclude that the base scenario just doesn't really work. And that's without going in depth on the spirit matters or specific resistances.<br /> <br /> Now, if you accept that Garou will have to die to make this work, then you can see it really is a dangerous situation for the Vampire involved which then goes a long way to explain why this doesn't just happen all the time.<br /> <br /> And neither of those conceits alter to core question of what the Garou then do after their Caern has been taken. War parties are a distinct possibility, supported by spirits and Fetishes, because that's how the Garou work. Ward vs Lupines and Spirits are remarkably weak and only really work as written in pure Vampire games because the STs say they do. The newer versions written at least have a non damage portion of the ritual that makes it more difficult. Older versions just did pathetic damage as a deterrent. But even still, those Wards can be broken. And I'm curious what the mechanic for fast casting them is that you mentioned. I was under the impression that Thaum Rituals were very much actual magic Rituals you had to set up and spend real time putting in place.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, usually, but one write-up of the Warding Circle rituals (can't remember which book... Rites of Blood? V20? Revised?) has a quick and dirty method. You need some Silver for Werewolves, Ashes for Ghosts/Zombies/Similar, some Blood for Vampires. They're rituals which are specifically written as taking 1 or 2 turns rather than 5 minutes per level.<br /> <br /> In this case it's a Ventrue Methesulah. The Methesulahs often have blood magic, and he was from Persia originally and his &quot;sister&quot; taught him Sadhana (the prestiged arts of Indian Ventrue). He has some pretty basic Obfuscate, Auspex at 6 (Ventrue Antitribu have Auspex), and Dominate, Presence and Fortitude are either at his max (9) or 1 below, don't have his sheet up.<br /> <br /> As for why the Setites haven't done that, it would ruin them over more than a month. This is a short-term victory for him. The Wards won't stand up to Theurgy or a War Pack. He's taking the time he needs to grieve, and then it's a coin-toss between greeting the sun (unlikely, he has Courage 5 but Road of Kings 2, so he's limited to Courage 2) and taking over England's Vampiric Courts (the Players are Anarchs and would probably have something to say about that). If he wanted to keep the place forever he probably would have approached more subtly and gathered support for the move first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 02-25-2017, 01:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T10:51:39-08:00","id":1054855,"title":"","content":"Well, Caern Spirits are powerful Jaggling spirits, so you are taking about entities that have very high levels of Rage, Gnosis, and Willpower (10 plus the level of the level of the Caern would be appropriate in my opinion) and that have very high levels of Essence (30 plus 30 times the level of the Caern would be appropriate in my opinion). Of course, Caern spirits are usually not involved in direct conflict, but I think it would make an exception to squish a Methusalah. Another thing to remember is that the Garou will summon a Celestial Avatar to destroy the Methuselah if they need to. When the Sun Avatar manifests in the Caern and embraces the Methusalah in a passionate embrace, you have one very dead Kindred.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T10:51:46-08:00","id":1054856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1054840#post1054840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I get that. A Mage with Spirit 3 or higher makes your best friends who you've bonded to for years into his puppets with ease. It feels... unfair. Thankfully he's squishy and far from invincible, you just need to outsmart him.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;with ease&quot; is a terrible understatement. But this point isn't terribly important.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1054844#post1054844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to close the book on all of this, Far Mastery and Auspex 5/6 are all he needs to Dominate them all into leaving from a good distance away. It just costs 2 points of Willpower, and can easily be combined with Group Dominate which is level 7 I believe. I don't want to have a pissing match, this isn't the point of this thread, it's supposed to be un fait accompli, but I'd like to settle the mechanical matter. <b>And at the end of the day it's all plot devices</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Emphasis mine. That line is all that matters here. When you try and rationalize it with quoting powers, you then open up the discussion to disagreement, because those powers don't get to just work because &quot;reasons&quot;. And you don't want the disagreement, so why bother?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1054846#post1054846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re-reading the last few posts, I am not sure if the 'werewolf spirit nerf' is because your PCs need to have counterplay, or because otherwise the Methuselah would have too difficult of a time taking over the caern.<br /> <br /> Having a crossover with werewolves is fine, but why even bother making them seem like WtA Garou? Why not just make them lupines, which are still dangerous, obviously, but vampires then don't have to deal with all the weird spirit magic (which you would be nerfing anyway; might as well jettison it for simplicity's sake). Also, if you need to nerf the Garou so that your players can more easily interact with them, that is fine. If you need to weaken them in order for your crazy McGuffin vampire to beat them, that is fine too, but you don't need our input at that point, since we are talking less about how werewolves as WtA players would run them, and more like the watered-down lupines of VtM (which, again, is fine, but this discrepancy might explain why you are getting a fair amount of pushback on the specifics of this scenario).</div> </div> </div> </div>This. All of this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1054847#post1054847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> A Master Thaumaturge could slowly corrupt the spirit and twist it to a new purpose. A group with Spirit Thaumaturgy could pull it off. Alternatively, I'm musing on some BSDs or Wyrm-tainted Mages/Sorcerers offering to assist him in exchange for access to the shrine (calling him their Prince, showing respect etc.).</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, you don't understand or even want to understand the setting. So more or less do whatever you want and ignore the WtA books. Why ask for input if you are then going to argue why none of the input matters?<br /> <br /> Admittedly, this is a bit snarky but: tossing the name Red Talons out there doesn't make your Lupines into Garou. As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3695_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3695\" data-vbnamecard=\"3695\">The Laughing Stranger</a> said, you can weaken all of the spirits and the Garou to fit your story and that is fine. It's your story and things will work the way you need to. But (seemingly) arguing that people who are telling you how the setting works don't understand is....bizarre to me.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T10:52:58-08:00","id":1054857,"title":"","content":"You mentioned the tribe of Whippoorwill. Perhaps just Occam's Razor that crap and sic some Black Spiral Dancers on the problem. They could even out the spiritual aspect of the fight and let the Methuselah do his thing. I think that might be a bit of a cleaner solution that having a pet bloodbound mage and then you don't really have to tinker overly much with the specifics of the caern defense. You can just assume the vile Theurges of the Black Spiral Dancers are sapping the powers of the spirits, making them less vigilant or what have you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T10:56:34-08:00","id":1054859,"title":"","content":"And this thread really belongs in the VtM forum because it does not respect the Lore or the Rules concerning the Fera (it is basically a thread of 'guess what cool things my Methuselah can do with VtM rules if I ignore WtA rules').","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T10:58:36-08:00","id":1054861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1054859#post1054859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And this thread really belongs in the VtM forum because it does not respect the Lore or the Rules concerning the Fera (it is basically a thread of 'guess what cool things my Methuselah can do with VtM rules if I ignore WtA rules').</div> </div> </div> </div> I so rarely agree with you, but this actually made me laugh. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T11:01:09-08:00","id":1054866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1054859#post1054859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And this thread really belongs in the VtM forum because it does not respect the Lore or the Rules concerning the Fera (it is basically a thread of 'guess what cool things my Methuselah can do with VtM rules if I ignore WtA rules').</div> </div> </div> </div>This has happened because repeatedly people have ignored my requests to focus on the response. I stated in the OP and twice after that my interest is in what a group of WTA Werewolves do after a Caern is stolen from them. Respondents asked for specifics and focused on mechanics. Respondents made it pretty toxic even as I tried to nudge it back on track. See the problem here?<br /> <br /> Rather than focusing on how people respond to event, no one can resist leaping headfirst into crossover mechanics arena.<br /> <br /> And so I ask VTM players what a group of &quot;lupines&quot; (who are Random RPG encounters with dots and no personality or real character to them) do, great. Wonderful.<br /> <br /> And seriously, I've given the Garou of the city and the surrounding countryside quite a lot of effort, I've got two named NPCs who are Silver Fangs and I've got a group of Red Talons migrating after this attack, I'm simply not interested in the PCs asking me why these spirits don't just obliterate Elysium or tip the Werewolves off about everything. I do this with crossovers. Wraiths? Yes. Arcanois? No. Shadows? If we have time, probably no. Spirits? Yes. Spirits being Smoke Alarms? No. Gifts? Yes, but within limits.<br /> <br /> These are the compromises you make. And I'm exhausted by accusations of neutering them when I'm literally saying &quot;hey maybe it's ambitious to port over 8 systems at once, I should simplify where I can while keeping The Good Stuff.&quot; I brush over mechanics and use plot devices because the alternative is sheer madness. And it's nice to talk about the abuse of Metis, the human-hating of the Red Fangs and inter-tribal conflicts without getting bogged down in the really niche parts of the lore which Vampire players and characters won't have any investment in. Would &quot;the Elder who you accidentally woke up attacked a Cairn and a sun spirit killed him&quot; be a good climax? Would &quot;he took over a Cairn but some spirits burned him alive&quot; be a poignant end to a major antagonist? No? Good.<br /> <br /> So I come here asking for the Good Stuff, and I get a nice big fat serving of antagonism. Thank you to those who actually answered my OP since it's given me some ideas on how to move forward, I'm imagining the PCs discovering the remains of the Winter Wolf ritual and getting some feels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 02-25-2017, 02:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T11:06:12-08:00","id":1054868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1054866#post1054866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Rather than focusing on how people respond to event, no one can resist leaping headfirst into crossover mechanics arena.</div> </div> </div> </div>You actually did get some responses (at least 3) specifically for what you requested (mine included). Hopefully that proves helpful.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T11:08:22-08:00","id":1054871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1054868#post1054868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You actually did get some responses (at least 3) specifically for what you requested (mine included). Hopefully that proves helpful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. And I thanked you all in that post if you read down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T11:10:35-08:00","id":1054872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1054857#post1054857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You mentioned the tribe of Whippoorwill. Perhaps just Occam's Razor that crap and sic some Black Spiral Dancers on the problem. They could even out the spiritual aspect of the fight and let the Methuselah do his thing. I think that might be a bit of a cleaner solution that having a pet bloodbound mage and then you don't really have to tinker overly much with the specifics of the caern defense. You can just assume the vile Theurges of the Black Spiral Dancers are sapping the powers of the spirits, making them less vigilant or what have you.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a nice idea. So he's able to take the Cairn because others laid the way for him, hinting at a greater darkness. The Kinfolk NPC can mention that him taking the Cairn should have been impossible, teasing the idea of a Bigger Bad messing with things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T11:14:34-08:00","id":1054875,"title":"","content":"Well, when a crossover situation is presented on the WtA forum, it is generally expected that WtA Lore and WtA Rules will be primary. Methuselahs are probably not going to go full frontal on a Sept of Garou. They will manipulate human institutions to make life unbearable on the Garou until either the Garou abandon the area or the Garou get themselves killed. When the Garou are gone, then the Methuselah will move in and corrupt the Caern spirit to create their ideal spiritual hellhole, probably with the help of Black Spiral Dancers or Nephandi that he bullied into service.<br /> <br /> After they have been driven out of their Caern, I would suggest the Garou learn about the attempts to corrupt the Caern spirit (perhaps from dreams messages sent by the Caern spirit itself). An entire campaign could be built around the Garou gaining the allies necessary to save the Caern spirit from corruption before it is too late, with the Garou having to make alliances with many creatures they would rather kill. Methuselah Kindred tend to have ancient enemies among the Kindred, so the Garou may be forced to ally with ancient Kindred to destroy the Methuselah. Its Black Spiral Dancer servants are the enemies of all Gaian Fera, so the Garou may be forced to ally with Bastet, Corax, Gurahl, and Nuwisha to regain the lost Caern. Its Nephandi servants are the enemies of all Tradition Mages, so the Garou may be forced to ally with members of the Cult of Ecstasy, Dreamspeakers, Order of Hermes, and the Verbena to regain the lost Caern. In effect, the stealing of the Caern can be a trigger for a local Grand Alliance that would take a dozen game sessions to form and would result in a series of epic battles that would take a dozen game sessions to finish. Of course, it would have to be a level 5 Caern to justify that level of effort, but it would make a great campaign.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T11:16:07-08:00","id":1054876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1054856#post1054856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, you don't understand or even want to understand the setting. So more or less do whatever you want and ignore the WtA books. Why ask for input if you are then going to argue why none of the input matters?<br /> <br /> Admittedly, this is a bit snarky but: tossing the name Red Talons out there doesn't make your Lupines into Garou. As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3695_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3695\" data-vbnamecard=\"3695\">The Laughing Stranger</a> said, you can weaken all of the spirits and the Garou to fit your story and that is fine. It's your story and things will work the way you need to. But (seemingly) arguing that people who are telling you how the setting works don't understand is....bizarre to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seriously? This is pretty disingenuous. Firstly you're assuming that I am clueless about the Lore when I'm simply making compromises like &quot;spirits aren't guard dogs&quot;, &quot;werewolves don't have subtle underdog powers&quot;. And the input I'm arguing against is input I specifically asked to be left out of the responses in my OP.<br /> <br /> Oh wonderful. We've gone into <i>that</i> territory.<br /> <br /> &quot;oh, you say you're trying to do all of these things, but I <b><i>bet</i></b> you can't get past some arbitrary gate-keeping. Quick, what was the length of the in-seam of the first BSD to fall to the wyrm?!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T11:18:22-08:00","id":1054878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1054866#post1054866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This has happened because repeatedly people have ignored my requests to focus on the response. I stated in the OP and twice after that my interest is in what a group of WTA Werewolves do after a Caern is stolen from them. Respondents asked for specifics and focused on mechanics. Respondents made it pretty toxic even as I tried to nudge it back on track. See the problem here?<br /> <br /> Rather than focusing on how people respond to event, no one can resist leaping headfirst into crossover mechanics arena.</div> </div> </div> </div>Two ideas for next time:<br /> 1) I'd recommend not even bringing up the mechanics or the &quot;To Do&quot; list next time, in your original post. Editing your OP as an example:<br /> So hypothetically, a Methesulah wakes up and tries to reclaim some site of importance to him, which is a sacred place to &quot;the lupines&quot;, not that they care obviously. S/he manages to run the Garou out of the Caern with tails between legs (leave the &quot;How&quot; up to me, it's not the purpose of my questions).<br /> <br /> How would a group of Garou and Kinfolk respond to being kicked out of their Caern? We're assuming that something is stopping them from just attacking the Elder during the day.<br /> <br /> ...and then on with the rest of your post. I'm not saying you did wrong by mentioning how, what stats/abilities, etc. But if people have those figures to argue over, they're likely to. And that brings me to #2!<br /> <br /> 2) You engaged in response to the arguing, and weren't exactly immune to it yourself. It sounds like you're frustrated, so just going to bluntly say that I'm not finger pointing, but that it takes two to tango, right? So, if you've set things up like #1, you have so much of an easier time to say, &quot;No, really, I'm not even going to discuss the &quot;hows&quot; because arguing about the mechanics isn't the point.&quot; To your credit, yeah, you did try to steer it back a couple times, but it's so much easier to do that if you don't provide Debate Fodder in the first place.<br /> <br /> Either way, good luck running your game! I hope it's all sorts of intriguing fun. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> ETA:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1054872#post1054872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a nice idea. So he's able to take the Cairn because others laid the way for him, hinting at a greater darkness. The Kinfolk NPC can mention that him taking the Cairn should have been impossible, teasing the idea of a Bigger Bad messing with things.</div> </div> </div> </div>I forgot I wanted to add something onto this, 'cause I was kind of pondering the &quot;What if...?&quot; when you mentioned BSDs as well. Whose to say they (the BSDs) don't have some kind of twisted Fetish to their aid, too? A wolf larynx that, when activated and whine-howled through, incites a Fox Frenzy, or something like that. Obviously there are details to work out, but if you have BSDs at the ready, you have a crap-ton of options to help you get around any mechanical fudgery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12777,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12777-wakuwa","user":"Wakuwa","date":". 02-25-2017, 02:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12777-wakuwa","name":"Wakuwa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12777_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T11:24:36-08:00","id":1054883,"title":"","content":"I'm getting the feeling that people have responded negatively due to some projected feelings. It's a repeated behaviour I've noticed, and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11683\" data-vbnamecard=\"11683\">Aya Tari</a>'s post highlights those feelings.<br /> <br /> What I post:<br /> <br /> &quot;This thing has happened, Werewolves are humiliated, what do they do plz Werewolf players? Thx&quot;<br /> <br /> What some people read:<br /> <br /> &quot;Haha this Elder I'm playing vicariously through just GG-no-REed some shitty lupines, suck on that you losers.&quot;<br /> <br /> What I post:<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh, I'm toning down the omniscience of Spirits, making them more guides and teachers and not having them be like CCTV, since it would make all conflicts between Vampires and Werewolves very one-sided&quot;<br /> <br /> What some people read:<br /> <br /> &quot;Hahahahaha fuck spirits amirite?&quot;<br /> <br /> What I post:<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh, these are Red Talons&quot;<br /> <br /> What people read:<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh, these Loopines are&quot; <i>looks at smudged writing on hand</i> &quot;Red Tails&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T11:25:34-08:00","id":1054884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wakuwa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1054878#post1054878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Various Sensible-ness<br /> <br /> ETA:<br /> <br /> I forgot I wanted to add something onto this, 'cause I was kind of pondering the &quot;What if...?&quot; when you mentioned BSDs as well. Whose to say they (the BSDs) don't have some kind of twisted Fetish to their aid, too? A wolf larynx that, when activated and whine-howled through, incites a Fox Frenzy, or something like that. Obviously there are details to work out, but if you have BSDs at the ready, you have a crap-ton of options to help you get around any mechanical fudgery.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks man. And that's a cool idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T11:30:16-08:00","id":1054886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1054876#post1054876\" rel=\"nofollow\" 