 your post. I'm not saying you did wrong by mentioning how, what stats/abilities, etc. But if people have those figures to argue over, they're likely to. And that brings me to #2!<br /> <br /> 2) You engaged in response to the arguing, and weren't exactly immune to it yourself. It sounds like you're frustrated, so just going to bluntly say that I'm not finger pointing, but that it takes two to tango, right? So, if you've set things up like #1, you have so much of an easier time to say, &quot;No, really, I'm not even going to discuss the &quot;hows&quot; because arguing about the mechanics isn't the point.&quot; To your credit, yeah, you did try to steer it back a couple times, but it's so much easier to do that if you don't provide Debate Fodder in the first place.<br /> <br /> <u>Either way, good luck running your game! I hope it's all sorts of intriguing fun</u>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Good stuff here, but agreeing with the last (emphasis mine) bit particularly.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T11:40:38-08:00","id":1054891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How would a group of Garou and Kinfolk respond to being kicked out of their Caern? We're assuming that something is stopping them from just attacking the Elder during the day. </div> </div> </div>Black Spiral Dancers can defend it... I am sure nothing will happen... there is literally no problem a posse of twisted inbred werewolves can't solve!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11620_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11620\" data-vbnamecard=\"11620\">twig</a> mentioned this being something like a blaze of self-destructive glory for the Methuselah in question, right? If I were a Black Spiral Dancer, that sounds pretty appealing. Crazy old vampire wants help attacking your enemies and then he wanders off and maybe dies after greeting the next sunrise. Sounds like there is now a free caern up for grabs! Hell, if I could ensure the vampire didn't survive past the short term, I'd jump at a chance like that. Might make things more interesting down the road for your PCs, having a Black Spiral Hive in proximity. Especially if the Dancers there were not overtly threatening from the get go, but they become more and more of a problem for the local Kindred.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T14:31:25-08:00","id":1054942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1054891#post1054891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Black Spiral Dancers can defend it... I am sure nothing will happen... there is literally no problem a posse of twisted inbred werewolves can't solve!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11620_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11620\" data-vbnamecard=\"11620\">twig</a> mentioned this being something like a blaze of self-destructive glory for the Methuselah in question, right? If I were a Black Spiral Dancer, that sounds pretty appealing. Crazy old vampire wants help attacking your enemies and then he wanders off and maybe dies after greeting the next sunrise. Sounds like there is now a free caern up for grabs! Hell, if I could ensure the vampire didn't survive past the short term, I'd jump at a chance like that. Might make things more interesting down the road for your PCs, having a Black Spiral Hive in proximity. Especially if the Dancers there were not overtly threatening from the get go, but they become more and more of a problem for the local Kindred.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm aware of all of the Lore-based reasons for defending Caerns, and what Mages can get from them, but in terms of the UNLIMITED POWAAHH!!! the BSDs can draw, what are we talking?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T15:37:18-08:00","id":1054964,"title":"","content":"Hm, how many BSD are there? I tend to run the Garou Nation at 15,000, but they only represent the Garou of Australia, Europe, North Africa, North America, South America, and West Asia. Ater much consideration, I think that there should be another 3,000 Garou who belong to the Ahadi and another 9,000 Garou who belong to the Beast Courts. I would say that the Black Spiral Dancers would be another 3,000 Garou, but that is just my opinion.<br /> <br /> Of course, Black Spiral Dancers can breed Garou quite quickly because they do not mind Metis, so something like 50% of Black Spiral Dancers are probably Metis (45% are probably Homid and 5% are probably Lupus). Metis survive because they are naturally born Crinis, so they can survive the abuse that would kill a Homid or Lupus Garou before their first change. While they are infertile, adult male Metis Black Spiral Dancers probably participate in the 'boots call' raids that leave female humans and female wolves traumatized just for the sadistic pleasure of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T19:45:45-08:00","id":1055045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1054942#post1054942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm aware of all of the Lore-based reasons for defending Caerns, and what Mages can get from them, but in terms of the UNLIMITED POWAAHH!!! the BSDs can draw, what are we talking?</div> </div> </div> </div>Black Spiral Dancers turn caerns into hives, taking advantage of the low Gauntlet and perverting the Gaian energies of the place to their own end. Hives allow for the summoning of powerful spirits, and the bestowment of specific benefits tied to the nature of the hive/caern. The BSDs might be interested in targeting the Gaians there, maybe capturing some of the fleeing Garou. Alternatively, they might be primarily interested in bringing the caern's totem into the Wyrm's service, or even performing the Rite of the Flayed God to destroy and skin it, stealing its power and investing it into a chosen Dancer, which can make that particular Garou Bad News, indeed.<br /> <br /> By the way, hives are hideous, frightful places, haunted by powerful evil spirits and crawling with insane kinfolk and werewolves and possessed. The vile goings-on in a hive should impress Tzimisce and make just about everyone else simultaneously vomit <i>and</i> shit themselves.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":".  What I am getting at is that most vampires would not be thrilled about having a hive around, but hey, them's the breaks. 02-25-2017, 10:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T21:39:06-08:00","id":1055081,"title":"","content":"What is the narrative point of having him come in, take over the Caern and make the Garou just leave? What story objective is obtained here that &quot;He comes in and murders the majority and only the youngest cubs escape&quot; wouldn't solve? I'm looking at Elder powers and it seem it seems like it would be easy enough to get people to frenzy at the wrong time, to challenge the wrong person etc. Basically get them weakened by fighting eachother then go in for the killing blow.<br /> <br /> So why does the Elder have to walk in and say &quot;Lupines go away!&quot; It seems like your more than willing to assume a dedicated long term plan for it(see far mastery) if they just wake up and are &quot;:driven to go to that spot&quot; then they aren't going to spend time hitting them with auspex far mastery tricks. If you want a scary elder who wakes up and fucks with the Garou.. why not make it a blood bath? What purpose is there in game for him not to kill the majority?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T00:05:57-08:00","id":1055115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1055081#post1055081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the narrative point of having him come in, take over the Caern and make the Garou just leave? What story objective is obtained here that &quot;He comes in and murders the majority and only the youngest cubs escape&quot; wouldn't solve? I'm looking at Elder powers and it seem it seems like it would be easy enough to get people to frenzy at the wrong time, to challenge the wrong person etc. Basically get them weakened by fighting eachother then go in for the killing blow.<br /> <br /> So why does the Elder have to walk in and say &quot;Lupines go away!&quot; It seems like your more than willing to assume a dedicated long term plan for it(see far mastery) if they just wake up and are &quot;:driven to go to that spot&quot; then they aren't going to spend time hitting them with auspex far mastery tricks. If you want a scary elder who wakes up and fucks with the Garou.. why not make it a blood bath? What purpose is there in game for him not to kill the majority?</div> </div> </div> </div>- he's fallen far down his Road but he has some semblance of honour.<br /> <br /> - the Lupines have kept the place where his beloved fell as a pristine memorial, deliberately or not.<br /> <br /> - getting them all to kill eachother? He's not a Malkavian, and he's not on the Path of the Tyrant. It wouldn't suit his character.<br /> <br /> - the group of Lupus who were forced to leave are a useful narrative device that I have plans for.<br /> <br /> - when he leaves he doesn't intend for the BSDs to hold onto the place, but he could lose control of that. Regardless, he would prefer if the place stayed pristine and beautiful beyond his leaving.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 02-26-2017, 03:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T00:53:31-08:00","id":1055121,"title":"","content":"I doubt that he could find a better group of people for making sure that the place is beautiful and pristine than the Garou Nation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T01:24:17-08:00","id":1055131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1055121#post1055121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I doubt that he could find a better group of people for making sure that the place is beautiful and pristine than the Garou Nation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why he would most likely do away with the BSDs on his way out, having had plenty of time to observe their surface thoughts and their actions when he isn't present (Farsight is useful for this). Speaking of breeding... I'm wondering whether he would try and keep a young Metis cub. I know they're allergic to Vitae, but a BSD Metis raised from near-birth or young childhood by a Methesulah would be a dangerous thing indeed.<br /> <br /> Oh, and the rules for the Gnosis roll to get a peaceful death when embraced, do those apply to BSDs? Since they've succumbed to a Wyrmish existence, do they make the roll or not?<br /> <br /> I can't see this Elder being long for this world. He isn't really 100% up-to-date on modern armaments and tactics, and someone could just RPG him to death if they could get a hold of modern weaponry. You know that moment in Buffy where the Vampire says he can't be killed by mortal weapons, and she pulls out a rocket launcher? Yeah. That.<br /> <br /> I'm imagining a recently embraced teenage BSD being left in the wake of his destruction, and making him be <i>not totally batshit insane </i>and <i>also not a Wight</i> being a big aim of the Players, who would probably end up needing to put it down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T08:17:48-08:00","id":1055248,"title":"","content":"Anything with Gnosis gets the roll, even BSD, so they chance of a random Abomination is low (of course, he could just work the numbers and attempt to Embrace dozens of BSDs over a few months until one of them takes).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T08:32:36-08:00","id":1055251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1055248#post1055248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anything with Gnosis gets the roll, even BSD, so they chance of a random Abomination is low (of course, he could just work the numbers and attempt to Embrace dozens of BSDs over a few months until one of them takes).</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like Abominations are underexplored. Obviously there have to be HUGE downsides to avoid it becoming a source of chagrin for all involved, but the idea of submitting to the Wyrm so totally is kind of neat. I don't like the idea of Abominations being inferior in Morality terms. It would be simpler to revert their Self-Control to 1 and give them the Brujah flaw. They're haunted by Banes and lose all Gifts, they keep their Forms but they are turned on by Blood. They keep Rage (spent in all ways but switching forms) but lose Gnosis.<br /> <br /> If they aren't a BSD or similarly open to Wyrm taint, they gain the Depression flaw and their Willpower regeneration is heavily nerfed. Sleep doesn't restore Willpower, and fulfilling their nature only works if they succeed in a coin toss. Those who are open to Wyrm taint and don't take the Depression flaw gain a supernatural flaw such as the Samedi Clan Weakness.<br /> <br /> They join Path of Humanity, or possibly an alterantive if they were inhumane enough in life. BSDs might take the Hierarchy of Wyrm Taint.<br /> <br /> Any Changing Breed can be embraced, however the odds of a Vampire ever even MEETING a Rokea or anything of that sort are low. Most who are embraced go to greet the sun, or go on a series of suicide missions for their Breed.<br /> <br /> The Gnosis roll would stay RAW to make them even more extra rare, but you could say that those who willingly submit to the embrace can increase the difficulty of the Gnosis roll.<br /> <br /> Basically I wouldn't want them to be unable to increase their Willpower or Path or their Virtues. Just stack the odds against them, the way it works with Vampires in general. They aren't naturally evil, but their tragic nature drives them towards being dehumanized. Make that true but more-so for any Garou or Fera who get embraced and don't die.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 02-26-2017, 11:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T10:08:23-08:00","id":1055299,"title":"","content":"Whatever works in your games, but I think Abominations are actually well explored for how uncommon they are (the average Fera with Gnosis 5 has a 16% chance of becoming Abominations when Embraced). First, Kindred have to find the Garou. Second, they have to defeat the Garou. Third, they have to subdue rather than kill the Garou. Fourth, they have to Embrace the Garou. I doubt that more than one-in-twenty-four hundred Garou are Abominations, so there might be a baker's dozen Garou Abominations globally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T10:36:30-08:00","id":1055306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1055299#post1055299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whatever works in your games, but I think Abominations are actually well explored for how uncommon they are (the average Fera with Gnosis 5 has a 16% chance of becoming Abominations when Embraced). First, Kindred have to find the Garou. Second, they have to defeat the Garou. Third, they have to subdue rather than kill the Garou. Fourth, they have to Embrace the Garou. I doubt that more than one-in-twenty-four hundred Garou are Abominations, so there might be a baker's dozen Garou Abominations globally.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I agree they should be exceptionally rare. But two things annoy me:<br /> <br /> - They can never regain permanent Willpower or Humanity or Virtues, if they lose a dot it's gone forever and they can't upgrade them. This feels kind of unnecessary in my opinion, as it's making things Impossible rather than simply Difficult or more difficult. Plus it feels a tad defeatist. It isn't a target to overcome, it isn't something you can have any hope for. Abominations are presented as being this sad angry thing with zero hope, but I'd argue that a sad angry thing with a glimmer, a fantasy of hope is even more cruel.<br /> <br /> - Lots of Breeds have &quot;um, well, a spirit says they can't&quot; attached, which adds the question of why the hell the Powers That Be let abominations exist at all. The Foxes and Ravens struck bargains to be spared the embrace, and that feels... odd. If they can do it, it opens a can of wyrms. For example, why don't Garou Abominations get burnt in moonlight by Luna's scorn? Helios is making extra doubly sure to char-grill every Corax Abomination. Especially odd is that the Ananasi can't be Embraced. You'd think they'd take to it, being natural blood-drinkers from birth.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 02-26-2017, 01:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T10:49:09-08:00","id":1055309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1055299#post1055299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whatever works in your games, but I think Abominations are actually well explored for how uncommon they are (the average Fera with Gnosis 5 has a 16% chance of becoming Abominations when Embraced). First, Kindred have to find the Garou. Second, they have to defeat the Garou. Third, they have to subdue rather than kill the Garou. Fourth, they have to Embrace the Garou. I doubt that more than one-in-twenty-four hundred Garou are Abominations, so there might be a baker's dozen Garou Abominations globally.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fifth, the abomination has to not commit suicide after they lose thier connection to the spiritual. Even kinfolk have a high percentage of suicide after becoming vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T10:59:38-08:00","id":1055316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1055309#post1055309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fifth, the abomination has to not commit suicide after they lose thier connection to the spiritual. Even kinfolk have a high percentage of suicide after becoming vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, I'm fully aware that most will kill their &quot;sire&quot;, say their goodbyes and walk to meet the sun. If that. Just seeing their family again might be too much. Alternatively they torture their Sire for knowledge of the location of other Vampires and run in Crinos to do one last service to Gaia before gladly meeting the sun. That's why I said many would do that :P<br /> <br /> Reasons they wouldn't, however? Courage. Facing the sun is a ridiculous act of courage which most Werewolves would pass naturally, since the depression and &quot;what have I become&quot; definitely help. But if they fail the first time, or worse botch (costing them a dot of courage) they will feed, and once they've fed that changes things. I mean it couldn't hurt to keep killing Vampires. Be a dark servant of Gaia. You're in control of course, you can handle this. Just a few more leeches dead and you'll face the sun. Promise. And slowly days become weeks, and they start to get a taste for Diablerie, the power that comes with it, and those whispers from Banes in the night become just a bit more tempting...<br /> <br /> Remember that Werewolves have zero clue about Diablerie, zero education in being a Vampire. They'll only feed from lower animals and leeches by preference, but that leads to Diablerie and Diablerie tanks your Path rating regardless of Path (well there are a bunch of exceptions but eating someone's soul tends to destabilize things) and before you know it their Path rating would be low enough that all of their Virtues would be limited (can't roll higher than your Path rating), and this would mean a monstrosity with Virtues as low as 1, and at that point you're a Wight in the making or a highly dangerous tool of the Wyrm, or a ripe convert to Darker Powers (such as the Baali, Setites...).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 02-26-2017, 02:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T11:34:56-08:00","id":1055324,"title":"","content":"This whole abomination topic reminds me of a Vampire Kinfolk character idea I had. It was suppose to be an NPC in one of my vampire games, but none of the players showed interest in him.<br /> <br /> Paul Revere was a Silversmith in real life. In my oWoD game, I had him be a Silver Fang Kinfolk Klaivesmith. Unfortunately for poor Paul, a passing Anarchist Toreador was impressed by his work and embraced him. Kindred Paul Revere ends up getting in all sorts of crazy hi-jinks during the American Revolution (including his infamous Midnight Ride). At the end of the war, he kills his Anarchist Sire and joins the Camerilla. He is a high ranking Vampire in *name of city here*.<br /> <br /> Doubly unfortunate for poor Paul, his Silver Fang descendants never forgot about him. The two Klaives he forged before his embrace are still wielded by his Silver Fang Family. When one passes to a new Garou, they are told the story of Paul Revere and the stain on their family honor. Every so often, a pack of Silver Lupines come to the city to hunt Paul down. None have killed him yet as he avoids facing them. Paul has been a vampire long enough to learn that a coward lives to see another sunset.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 02-26-2017, 02:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T11:40:23-08:00","id":1055325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1055324#post1055324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This whole abomination topic reminds me of a Vampire Kinfolk character idea I had. It was suppose to be an NPC in one of my vampire games, but none of the players showed interest in him.<br /> <br /> Paul Revere was a Silversmith in real life. In my oWoD game, I had him be a Silver Fang Kinfolk Klaivesmith. Unfortunately for poor Paul, a passing Anarchist Toreador was impressed by his work and embraced him. Kindred Paul Reeve ends up getting in all sorts of crazy hi-jinks during the American Revolution (including his infamous Midnight Ride). At the end of the war, he kills his Anarchist Sire and joins the Camerilla. He is a high ranking Vampire in *name of city here*.<br /> <br /> Doubly unfortunate for poor Paul, his Silver Fang descendants never forgot about him. The two Klaives he forged before his embrace are still wielded by his Silver Fang Family. When one passes to a new Garou, they are told the story of Paul Reeve and the stain on their family honor. Every so often, a pack of Silver Lupines come to the city to hunt Paul down. None have killed him yet as he avoids facing them. Paul has been a vampire long enough to learn that a coward lives to see another sunset.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a great concept! I was always intrigued by Kinfolk embraces and Werewolf embraces. I feel like it could have been treated a bit more like Maeghar. So Werewolves become Abominations, Kinfolk (homid kinfolk, if you want Vampire Wolves running around... no) become the Wolf equivalent of Maeghar. So they get Protean as in-clan as a replacement of one of their in-clan Disciplines, and they get a vulnerability to silver as an additional weakness. If they're kin to some other breed they can choose something else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T11:50:13-08:00","id":1055330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1055325#post1055325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a great concept! I was always intrigued by Kinfolk embraces and Werewolf embraces. I feel like it could have been treated a bit more like Maeghar. So Werewolves become Abominations, Kinfolk (homid kinfolk, if you want Vampire Wolves running around... no) become the Wolf equivalent of Maeghar. So they get Protean as in-clan as a replacement of one of their in-clan Disciplines, and they get a vulnerability to silver as an additional weakness. If they're kin to some other breed they can choose something else.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's been a while since I ran a vampire game and Paul's character sheet is long gone. He was a Toreador, but I believe I had either Animalism and/or Protean on his sheet. He still paid out of clan costs for those disciplines though. Kindred Paul had a pretty decent information network, like his real life counterpart. Animalism may have played a part in his information network.<br /> <br /> Also, I should note, Paul has a third Klaive among his processions. He keeps it in his attic as a memento of his pre-Embrace life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 02-26-2017, 02:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T12:51:19-08:00","id":1055352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1055251#post1055251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Gnosis roll would stay RAW to make them even more extra rare, but you could say that those who willingly submit to the embrace can increase the difficulty of the Gnosis roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you already know whether they are willing or not doesn't matter. Otherwise a few dots Presence would make Abominations much more common.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1055251#post1055251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> They aren't naturally evil, but their tragic nature drives them towards being dehumanized. Make that true but more-so for any Garou or Fera who get embraced and don't die.</div> </div> </div> </div> Fera weren't really &quot;humanized&quot; to begin with. Though I agree their inherent nature mixed with the embrace makes for a tragic story.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1055299#post1055299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> the average Fera with Gnosis 5 has a 16% chance of becoming Abominations when Embraced</div> </div> </div> </div>I think your numbers are off. I'm looking at a WoD probability sheet and I'm showing only a 2.1% chance of botching with 5 dice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1055251#post1055251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> First, Kindred have to find the Garou. Second, they have to defeat the Garou. Third, they have to subdue rather than kill the Garou. Fourth, they have to Embrace the Garou. I doubt that more than one-in-twenty-four hundred Garou are Abominations, so there might be a baker's dozen Garou Abominations globally.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreeing with all of the situational difficulties and from there I would say the number of active abominations is probably in the single digits (I suppose the difference between that and a baker's dozen is trivial though <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1055306#post1055306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> - They can never regain permanent Willpower or Humanity or Virtues, if they lose a dot it's gone forever and they can't upgrade them. This feels kind of unnecessary in my opinion, as it's making things Impossible rather than simply Difficult or more difficult. Plus it feels a tad defeatist. It isn't a target to overcome, it isn't something you can have any hope for. Abominations are presented as being this sad angry thing with zero hope, but I'd argue that a sad angry thing with a glimmer, a fantasy of hope is even more cruel.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't mind that rule, but in the end it doesn't matter too much. Change whichever rules you feel like.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1055306#post1055306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> - Lots of Breeds have &quot;um, well, a spirit says they can't&quot; attached, which adds the question of why the hell the Powers That Be let abominations exist at all. The Foxes and Ravens struck bargains to be spared the embrace, and that feels... odd.</div> </div> </div> </div>The foxes have a few odd rules about them, so that one doesn't bother me so much. The Corax make a ton of sense. And I don't think they specifically struck any sort of bargain so much as Helios is so anti-Vampire (by both game's lore accounts) that is just isn't meant to be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1055306#post1055306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If they can do it, it opens a can of wyrms. For example, why don't Garou Abominations get burnt in moonlight by Luna's scorn? Helios is making extra doubly sure to char-grill every Corax Abomination. Especially odd is that the Ananasi can't be Embraced. You'd think they'd take to it, being natural blood-drinkers from birth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Luna isn't spiritually opposed on a fundamental level to the Vampires who are creature of the night? Just about all of the Fera vulnerable to Silver (and so aligned with Luna) can be embraced. Whereas all of the others cannot. Maybe it's their tie to the night/moon that allows the Embrace to have a possibility of taking hold. This would then explain the Ananasi as well since they lack that metaphysical link.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T22:23:27-08:00","id":1055538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1055115#post1055115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> - he's fallen far down his Road but he has some semblance of honour.<br /> <br /> - the Lupines have kept the place where his beloved fell as a pristine memorial, deliberately or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>What road is he on that he has honor but &quot;drive people from their sacred land that they would die for&quot; is acceptable? This is like walking into Mecca and telling all the Muslims to leave and never come back. .<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - getting them all to kill eachother? He's not a Malkavian, and he's not on the Path of the Tyrant. It wouldn't suit his character. </div> </div> </div>Elder levels of Dominate seem to be either &quot;Ranged&quot; or &quot;make people think they had theirown thoughts&quot; improvements on lesser powers. This is on par with &quot;I command you to kill yourself&quot; and that's basically what will happen. They fall into Harano, they fall to the wyrm. They get challenged by others for hteir weakness. There is nothing in this that isn't pointlessly cruel and vindictive. Actually its more cruel and vindictive than killing them. Then at least they would have the honor of a warriors Death. <br /> <br /> SO Tyrant, Sin, Evil Revelations these are the sort of paths I'd imagine someone who tries this would be on or super low humanity.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - the group of Lupus who were forced to leave are a useful narrative device that I have plans for. </div> </div> </div><br /> in Such a way that a couple of cubs who survived his awesome killing spree would not?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - when he leaves he doesn't intend for the BSDs to hold onto the place, but he could lose control of that. Regardless, he would prefer if the place stayed pristine and beautiful beyond his leaving. </div> </div> </div>Then he shouldn't have walked in and did that because its going to get taken by a Hive. There's no &quot;take back&quot; from this. If he wanted to &quot;Leave only foot steps&quot; he's got dominate and Presence and Obfuscate he can have unlimited access without doing a thing to them. He's always &quot;that kinfolk we all like&quot; that &quot;everyone remembers&quot; etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T06:15:39-08:00","id":1055617,"title":"","content":"Yes, a Methuselah Kindred that manages to deceive everyone (including the local spirits into accepting him) would be very interesting. With elder levels of Disciplines, there could be some very interesting powers that extend the effects of Dominate, Obfuscate, and Presence into the Umbra. At ninth level, the effects might even work on Jagglings like Incarna Avatars.<br /> <br /> In that case, the 4th generation Kindred has probably always been at the Caern. He would maintain a high Humanity, would feed lightly on Human Kinfolk, and would be the secret protector of the Caern. Every night (except during the Moots), he would be found among his 'Kin', teaching children useful skills and training young Garou in mundane combat. When the Wyrm attacks, he becomes a terrible unseen presence that destroys any servant of the Wyrm who defiles his territory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T06:30:19-08:00","id":1055621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1055617#post1055617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, a Methuselah Kindred that manages to deceive everyone (including the local spirits into accepting him) would be very interesting. With elder levels of Disciplines, there could be some very interesting powers that extend the effects of Dominate, Obfuscate, and Presence into the Umbra. At ninth level, the effects might even work on Jagglings like Incarna Avatars.<br /> <br /> In that case, the 4th generation Kindred has probably always been at the Caern. He would maintain a high Humanity, would feed lightly on Human Kinfolk, and would be the secret protector of the Caern. Every night (except during the Moots), he would be found among his 'Kin', teaching children useful skills and training young Garou in mundane combat. When the Wyrm attacks, he becomes a terrible unseen presence that destroys any servant of the Wyrm who defiles his territory.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Shit. The Kindred may not even need to use Dominate/Presence after the first few generations. The Garou who are raised in this Sept wouldn't think anything of their undead &quot;kin&quot; because they have known him all of their life. The elders of the Sept would even see the vampire as a dear old uncle. They would protect his identity from visiting Garou.<br /> <br /> A bunch of Garou, who think you are family and will protect your with their lives? A whole Kinfolk community who would gladly offer a regular blood donation? Yeah, I could see a vampire kill any Wyrm spirits, other vampires, and Gaia knows what else to protect that particular herd.<br /> <br /> Now I imagine there may be some uppity ancestors who want the Kindred dead for leeching off their descendants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 02-27-2017, 09:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T07:04:21-08:00","id":1055634,"title":"","content":"Of course, if the Caern is in the Old World, the Methuselah may have been part of the life of the Caern for thousands of years and may have been Kinfolk when he was alive, so he might be on good terms with the Ancestors. Imagine a Silver Fang Caern in Ancient Gaul that was created before the founding of Rome. The Methuselah may have been one of the Human Kinfolk who participated in helping the Garou during the Rite that created the Caern and was Embraced by [Toreador] sometime after the creation of the Caern. For three thousand years, he would have been part of the life of that Caern and has been protecting his Herd from everything that the Wyrm and the Weaver could send against it. With a few tweaks (change the Methuselah from a 'he' to a 'she' and change the location of the Caern from Ancient Gaul to Ancient Greece), you could have the Methuselah being part of a Black Fury Caern. Heck, I could see that as a plausible survival strategy for the few Methuselah who maintain high levels of Humanity because it would be nearly impossible for younger Kindred to penetrate the defenses of the Caern.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 02-27-2017, 10:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T07:13:23-08:00","id":1055637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1055634#post1055634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, if the Caern is in the Old World, the Methuselah may have been part of the life of the Caern for thousands of years and may have been Kinfolk when he was alive, so he might be on good terms with the Ancestors. Imagine a Silver Fang Caern in Ancient Gaul that was created before the founding of Rome. The Methuselah may have been one of the Human Kinfolk who participated in helping the Garou during the Rite that created the Caern and was Embraced by [Toreador] sometime after the creation of the Caern. For three thousand years, he would have been part of the life of that Caern and has been protecting his Herd from everything that the Wyrm and the Weaver could send against it. With a few tweaks (change the Methuselah from a 'he' to a 'she' and change the location of the Caern from Ancient Gaul to Ancient Greece), you could have the Methuselah being part of a Black Fury Caern. Heck, I could see that as a plausible survival strategy for the few Methuselah who maintain high levels of Humanity because it would be nearly impossible for younger Kindred to penetrate the defenses of the Caern.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Kinfolk Kindred being on good terms with the ancestors would probably be true, but if I was using this in a werewolf game, I'd use piss off Ancestors to kick off plot. Don't want this Methuselah to be too snug in their little caern. <br /> <br /> This is the type of plot that creates Legendary Ranked Garou. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T08:36:50-08:00","id":1055661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1055637#post1055637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The Kinfolk Kindred being on good terms with the ancestors would probably be true, but if I was using this in a werewolf game, I'd use piss off Ancestors to kick off plot. Don't want this Methuselah to be too snug in their little caern.<br /> <br /> This is the type of plot that creates Legendary Ranked Garou. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm liking this. IMO the best Clan would be Ahrimane or some kind of Koldun. Ideally an Ahrimane with Koldunism. She's Grandmother, and her Disciplines cover up her lack of life signs and her high Path rating (Kings would work, especially Vizier since it promotes 'advising' (read: ruling) from the shadows) cover her Wyrm taint. She uses Spiritus to communicate with animal spirits, and she has advised the occupants of this level 5 Caern for... 1000 years? For bonus points she was Kinfolk before the embrace, making her a more believable individual RE backstory.<br /> <br /> Here's the real question. If a Garou discovered her true nature and killed her, would that be a loss of Wisdom or a gain of Valour?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T08:51:08-08:00","id":1055666,"title":"","content":"I would suggest Old Clan if you are looking at a Koldun, a 4th generation childer of Tzmisce that rejected Vicissitude. The question of killing the Kindred would be would they survive the outrage of the Sept? They just killed the Guardian of one of the most powerful Caerns on Earth, meaning that it is now vulnerable to the Wyrm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T08:53:02-08:00","id":1055667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1055661#post1055661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm liking this. IMO the best Clan would be Ahrimane or some kind of Koldun. Ideally an Ahrimane with Koldunism. She's Grandmother, and her Disciplines cover up her lack of life signs and her high Path rating (Kings would work, especially Vizier since it promotes 'advising' (read: ruling) from the shadows) cover her Wyrm taint. She uses Spiritus to communicate with animal spirits, and she has advised the occupants of this level 5 Caern for... 1000 years? For bonus points she was Kinfolk before the embrace, making her a more believable individual RE backstory.<br /> <br /> Here's the real question. If a Garou discovered her true nature and killed her, would that be a loss of Wisdom or a gain of Valour?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was intending that the Elders of the Sept know about the nature of Grandma Kindred. They grew up with her. She isn't like those other leeches. She's Kin. The Garou of the Sept believe she is in a symbiotic relationship with her. Of course, she is just a parasite feeding off the Sept just like any other Leech. <br /> <br /> There are two ways this could play out.<br /> <br /> One, the PCs are a pack of Outsiders coming in to Sept. They haven't been indoctrinated by old Grandma Kindred, but have been sent by an Ancestor spirit's cryptic message. The plot will involve uncovering what the fuck is going on and perhaps cleaning the sept out of the Kindred's corruption.<br /> <br /> Two, the PCs are a Pack of young Garou who grew up in the Sept. They know about Grandma Kindred, but haven't been trusted with the knowledge of what she truly is. As Fosterns, the pack had a bad experience with a group of vampires while visiting another Sept. They don't trust them and know how crafty they are. Ideally, this is a long campaign and Grandma Kindred is a minor NPC at first. The Vampire experience is a plot the PCs actually experienced. They come back to their home Sept and slowly realize something is wrong. Maybe go on a few spirit quests to meet the pissed off ancestor. When they find out about the true nature of Grandma Kindred, the PCs must decide if they want to continue to support Grandma or remove the vampire from their Caern.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T09:08:01-08:00","id":1055672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1055666#post1055666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would suggest Old Clan if you are looking at a Koldun, a 4th generation childer of Tzmisce that rejected Vicissitude. The question of killing the Kindred would be would they survive the outrage of the Sept? They just killed the Guardian of one of the most powerful Caerns on Earth, meaning that it is now vulnerable to the Wyrm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well Old Clan Tzimisce have a bond with Koldunism, yes, but the issue there is that Kupala is AT BEST the dark side of Gaia, and at worst it's a Demon or a shattered fragment of Gaia which has been infested with Wyrmish corruption.<br /> <br /> So in that case it would need to be &quot;Koldunism&quot;, but the source is Gaia rather than Kupala. She could have a unique Way or Kraina which relates to the Caern. I like Ahrimane since they have a special relationship with Spirits and they're an offshoot of the Gangrel, so it feels good. But either could work perfectly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T09:45:20-08:00","id":1055687,"title":"","content":"Ooh. Big question. Let's say this Grandmother thing works and she's a fixture of the Caern for ages. A Warrior is on their deathbed and they don't want to die. Would an embrace be acceptable? The Garou were big on obtaining the Rite from the Gurahl which would resurrect fallen warriors... then again, one trusted longstanding Kinfolk who has mastered their condition and lasted for centuries without any real incident is one thing. Letting them &quot;breed&quot;... no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T10:01:37-08:00","id":1055690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1055687#post1055687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ooh. Big question. Let's say this Grandmother thing works and she's a fixture of the Caern for ages. A Warrior is on their deathbed and they don't want to die. Would an embrace be acceptable? The Garou were big on obtaining the Rite from the Gurahl which would resurrect fallen warriors... then again, one trusted longstanding Kinfolk who has mastered their condition and lasted for centuries without any real incident is one thing. Letting them &amp;quot;breed&amp;quot;... no.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think Grandma would want the competition of another vampire, but maybe once she got lonely and embraced a favorite of hers. <br /> <br /> I know most Garou are &quot;allergic&quot; to vampire blood. Maybe though years of careful breeding, Grandma managed to breed a line of Garou she can Ghoul. That would make the Sept Elders a bigger threat because they are bound to grandma by more than familial loyalty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T10:06:58-08:00","id":1055693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1055690#post1055690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think Grandma would want the competition of another vampire, but maybe once she got lonely and embraced a favorite of hers.<br /> <br /> I know most Garou are &quot;allergic&quot; to vampire blood. Maybe though years of careful breeding, Grandma managed to breed a line of Garou she can Ghoul. That would make the Sept Elders a bigger threat because they are bound to grandma by more than familial loyalty.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well some aren't allergic, there are canonical Ghouled Werewolves. I'd say that Grandma would use Blood Magic to pull it off. If you wanted to twist it and make it darker, she's spread her blood into the water of the Caern to strengthen the plants, animals, kin and the Garou. Their little sub-tribe is EXCEPTIONALLY strong, and there are legends of how the water will heal wounded warriors and grant them temporary strength. With a powerful ritual she converts her blood to water (Way of Water based Rite) but it keeps the Ghouling effects. Those who drink the water have prolonged but not unlimited lifespans, and the plants are enormous and powerful, and highly nutritious.<br /> <br /> The PCs gain an &quot;extra dot of strength&quot; and age slowly. The Big Twist puts everything in perspective.<br /> <br /> As an alternative, she's pretending to be an Ananasi, not a Vampire. Hard to pull off, but not impossible.<br /> <br /> As a plot-starter, another Tribe or Sept or Pack claim that this Caern has &quot;fallen to the Wyrm&quot; and begin sabotaging things, trying to gather a War Pack. As a sad possible ending, Grandmother greets the sun to try and spare her family the War Pack, but this just leads to the environment beginning to die since it has become dependent on her blood. The rest of the chronicle is finding a way to restore the Caern's spirit and stop the decay of the wildlife.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 02-27-2017, 01:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T10:38:32-08:00","id":1055704,"title":"","content":"Hm, I do not think that the Ahrimane angle would work because the Ahrimanes are derived from the Sabbat and were founded during the 19th century in the southern USA (and they never got above the 8th generation anyway). If you want a Methusaluh, you really need to have them come from an established Clan (other than the Giovanni or the Tremere). Of course, an ancient Lhiannan might be a good alternative to an established Clan, but I do not think that they ever got above the 7th generation.<br /> <br /> Whatever her origin, the Methusalah might have been able to develop a type of blood magic that is similar to Koldunism but depends on developing a Spirit Pact with a Gaian Incarna rather than Kupala. It could be functionally identical to Koldunic Sorcery, though I would think that it would depend more on charming nature spirits rather than dominating nature spirits. I would think that one of the consequences of her connection to the Gaian Incarna would be to make her blood incapable of effecting anything protected by the Gaian Incarna (she could not bond, embrace, or ghoul Fera or Kinfolk).<br /> <br /> The reason why she would be accepted by the Garou is because she bears to mark of a Gaian Incarna. Regardless of her origin, she would be a powerful warrior of Gaia and would have been vetted by a Gaian Incarna. I would make it the Totem associated with the Caern and, as long as she slept within the borders of the Caern every night and maintained the terms of her Spirit Pact, her Spirit Pact would give her (Caern Level) in blood points upon awakening and immunity to the weaknesses of the Kindred while she was within the borders of the Caern until the next time that she slept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T10:46:02-08:00","id":1055710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1055704#post1055704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm, I do not think that the Ahrimane angle would work because the Ahrimanes are derived from the Sabbat and were founded during the 19th century in the southern USA (and they never got above the 8th generation anyway). If you want a Methusaluh, you really need to have them come from an established Clan (other than the Giovanni or the Tremere). Of course, an ancient Lhiannan might be a good alternative to an established Clan, but I do not think that they ever got above the 7th generation.<br /> <br /> Whatever her origin, the Methusalah might have been able to develop a type of blood magic that is similar to Koldunism but depends on developing a Spirit Pact with a Gaian Incarna rather than Kupala. It could be functionally identical to Koldunic Sorcery, though I would think that it would depend more on charming nature spirits rather than dominating nature spirits. I would think that one of the consequences of her connection to the Gaian Incarna would be to make her blood incapable of effecting anything protected by the Gaian Incarna (she could not bond, embrace, or ghoul Fera or Kinfolk).<br /> <br /> The reason why she would be accepted by the Garou is because she bears to mark of a Gaian Incarna. Regardless of her origin, she would be a powerful warrior of Gaia and would have been vetted by a Gaian Incarna. I would make it the Totem associated with the Caern and, as long as she slept within the borders of the Caern every night and maintained the terms of her Spirit Pact, her Spirit Pact would give her (Caern Level) in blood points upon awakening and immunity to the weaknesses of the Kindred while she was within the borders of the Caern until the next time that she slept.</div> </div> </div> </div>Read DAV20, the Ahrimane date back to the earliest years of the Viking civilization. The 19th Century Ahrimane were simply reawakening lost elements of their blood which were buried when the Ahrimane began calling themselves Gangrel and embracing men. The spiritual arts of South American mystics awoke their old roots and transformed a Gangrel back into an Ahrimane, who could transform other female Kindred.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T11:07:00-08:00","id":1055714,"title":"","content":"The amount of head shaking I've done reading these last few posts. And it isn't that the idea is implausible. I've had a similar character in a game. But that Vampire never went near the Caern if it could help it. It's one thing to have a mysterious entity that shows up occasionally to help. It's another to have said creature integrated into the Caern structure.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1055621#post1055621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Shit. The Kindred may not even need to use Dominate/Presence after the first few generations. The Garou who are raised in this Sept wouldn't think anything of their undead &quot;kin&quot; because they have known him all of their life. The elders of the Sept would even see the vampire as a dear old uncle. They would protect his identity from visiting Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>And they would get Rite of Gaia's Vengeful Teeth when they were found out eventually. This is pretty much the definition of not allowing a Caern to be violated.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1055621#post1055621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Now I imagine there may be some uppity ancestors who want the Kindred dead for leeching off their descendants.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;uppity ancestors&quot;? For not wanting their descendants working alongside a leech to protect their sacred places? If this was setup out in the open like this, the spirits would tell others all but immediately.<br /> The premise from further up of the Vampire in question hiding among the Kinfolk (probably off-Caern) works a lot better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1055661#post1055661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm liking this. IMO the best Clan would be Ahrimane or some kind of Koldun. Ideally an Ahrimane with Koldunism. She's Grandmother, and her Disciplines cover up her lack of life signs and her high Path rating (Kings would work, especially Vizier since it promotes 'advising' (read: ruling) from the shadows) cover her Wyrm taint. She uses Spiritus to communicate with animal spirits, and she has advised the occupants of this level 5 Caern for... 1000 years? For bonus points she was Kinfolk before the embrace, making her a more believable individual RE backstory.</div> </div> </div> </div>You would have to make up your own Blood Magic since Koldunism in very much Wyrm-tainted. You can use the system and just say it's from Gaian sources if you'd like, but it would still be very different from a metaphysical standpoint.<br /> Also, just toss out the idea of this happening at a high level Caern. That just isn't going to happen. There are too many powerful Spirits that show up to them and too much Garou (and other Fera) traffic. You'll want to have a max Level 3 for something like this.<br /> Oh...and Road of Kings is Wyrm tainted if you look at it from the WtA perspective (all Roads are). There are sometimes exceptions made for specific Roads/Paths for specific reasons, but I would never put Kings in there among them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1055661#post1055661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's the real question. If a Garou discovered her true nature and killed her, would that be a loss of Wisdom or a gain of Valour?</div> </div> </div> </div>They would get a large chunk of <u>both</u> Wisdom and Glory. Glory for killing the Vampire. Wisdom for uncovering a long running deceit. Truthfulness falls under Wisdom.<br /> Oh, and extra Wisdom and Honor Renown for essentially rescuing a Caern.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1055687#post1055687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ooh. Big question. Let's say this Grandmother thing works and she's a fixture of the Caern for ages. A Warrior is on their deathbed and they don't want to die. Would an embrace be acceptable? The Garou were big on obtaining the Rite from the Gurahl which would resurrect fallen warriors... then again, one trusted longstanding Kinfolk who has mastered their condition and lasted for centuries without any real incident is one thing. Letting them &quot;breed&quot;... no.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely not. And resurrection and the Embrace aren't even close to the same thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1055693#post1055693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well some aren't allergic, there are canonical Ghouled Werewolves.</div> </div> </div> </div> Not since early edition weirdness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1055693#post1055693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'd say that Grandma would use Blood Magic to pull it off. If you wanted to twist it and make it darker, she's spread her blood into the water of the Caern to strengthen the plants, animals, kin and the Garou. Their little sub-tribe is EXCEPTIONALLY strong, and there are legends of how the water will heal wounded warriors and grant them temporary strength. With a powerful ritual she converts her blood to water (Way of Water based Rite) but it keeps the Ghouling effects. Those who drink the water have prolonged but not unlimited lifespans, and the plants are enormous and powerful, and highly nutritious.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just no. Garou are very much about the natural cycle, and a Caern's inhabitants all living extended lifetimes will be noticed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1055693#post1055693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> As an alternative, she's pretending to be an Ananasi, not a Vampire. Hard to pull off, but not impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because an Ananasi is going to be any more welcome at a Caern? This goes into the Realm of a lot more obscure knowledge than just knowing about Garou.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1055693#post1055693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> As a plot-starter, another Tribe or Sept or Pack claim that this Caern has &quot;fallen to the Wyrm&quot; and begin sabotaging things, trying to gather a War Pack. As a sad possible ending, Grandmother greets the sun to try and spare her family the War Pack, but this just leads to the environment beginning to die since it has become dependent on her blood. The rest of the chronicle is finding a way to restore the Caern's spirit and stop the decay of the wildlife.</div> </div> </div> </div>So the environment is going to begin to die because it's been cut off from undead blood? How does that make any sense at all to you? Having a Vampire feeding off a Caern for ages and then having said Vampire disappear is going to do wonders for the area.<br /> <br /> <br /> So again, the premise of this idea is passable. But the Vampire has to be very careful to avoid stepping onto the Caern's Bawn. Because once they do, the ruse begins to fall apart. And if they are &quot;living&quot; openly among the Sept, then this is just going to be more of a tragic story since most of the Sept members are going to die when the Caern inevitably gets spear headed and taken over. This is the exact sort of thing that makes the Shadow Lord Judges of Doom necessary/respected among the Garou Nation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 02-27-2017, 02:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T11:53:52-08:00","id":1055720,"title":"","content":"Well, I am not disagreeing with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar805_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"805\" data-vbnamecard=\"805\">idpersona</a>, as the vast majority of Methuselah are just going to be too much of the Wyrm to be anything acceptable. For a Methuselah to be accepted by the Garou, she would have had to have served Gaia (and an Incarna) long enough to become something else, perhaps a Kami Kindred? The respect that the Garou have for the Kami might balance out their loathing of the Kindred, but we are really talking about a unique entity (who might end up transcending into an Incarna long before she became a Kami).<br /> <br /> Now, that being said, a Methuselah with high levels of Humanity or the Path of the Feral Heart (since that is treated as Humanity for the purposes of being considered to be a creature of the Wyrm according to the Vampire's Storyteller's Handbook: Revised, p. 137) could possibly masquerade as Kinfolk using elder levels of Dominate, Obfuscate, and Presence (especially if she had elder powers that worked on spirits). She would probably think that the local Bawn was her territory and the local Kinfolk were her Herd and, as long as she did not interfere too much with the local Garou, no one would suspect that anything was wrong (as she would not be considered to be a creature of the Wyrm with Humanity 7+ or the Path of the Feral Heart 7+). Now, if she fell below Humanity 7 or the Path of the Feral Heart 7, things would probably start to go wrong very, very quickly.<br /> <br /> I would probably require a sixth level elder power to allow a specific Discipline to work on Gafflings, a seventh level elder power to allow a specific Discipline to work on Jagglings, an eighth level elder power to allow a specific Discipline to work on Totem Avatars, and a ninth level elder power to allow a specific Discipline to work on Incarna (purchasing the higher level powers would not give you the capabilities of the lower level powers because they work on different spiritual 'frequencies'). While Obfuscate would work on anything trying to perceive you visually, you would need an Obfuscate 9 elder power to interfere with the spiritual perceptions of an Incarna. In the case of Dominate and Presence, you would have to be able to perceive a spirit to be able to benefit from using the elder powers. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T12:30:12-08:00","id":1055735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1055720#post1055720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well, I am not disagreeing with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar805_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"805\" data-vbnamecard=\"805\">idpersona</a>, as the vast majority of Methuselah are just going to be too much of the Wyrm to be anything acceptable. For a Methuselah to be accepted by the Garou, she would have had to have served Gaia (and an Incarna) long enough to become something else, perhaps a Kami Kindred? The respect that the Garou have for the Kami might balance out their loathing of the Kindred, but we are really talking about a unique entity (who might end up transcending into an Incarna long before she became a Kami).</div> </div> </div> </div>So at least for the game I ran, the local Garou though the Vampire was a Kami. They only encountered him once every few decades, if that. Once it showed up to help defend the Caern from an assault, but disappeared before the fight actually ended so they didn't have time to really examine it at all. I think 1 Elder found out, but kept it to herself since there wasn't anything to be done about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1055720#post1055720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Now, that being said, a Methuselah with high levels of Humanity or the Path of the Feral Heart (since that is treated as Humanity for the purposes of being considered to be a creature of the Wyrm according to the Vampire's Storyteller's Handbook: Revised, p. 137) could possibly masquerade as Kinfolk using elder levels of Dominate, Obfuscate, and Presence (especially if she had elder powers that worked on spirits). She would probably think that the local Bawn was her territory and the local Kinfolk were her Herd and, as long as she did not interfere too much with the local Garou, no one would suspect that anything was wrong (as she would not be considered to be a creature of the Wyrm with Humanity 7+ or the Path of the Feral Heart 7+). Now, if she fell below Humanity 7 or the Path of the Feral Heart 7, things would probably start to go wrong very, very quickly.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, I can agree with this approach a lot more than the &quot;known ally&quot; approach. Though it still gets to be an extremely dangerous area if the Vampire is feeding off of the Kinfolk. There is no reason not to feed elsewhere if you are this powerful. Doing so just invites unwanted attention. And if the Vampire does in fact view the Kinfolk as their family, then that's just more of a reason to feed from others.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1054739-how-do-proud-warriors-respond-to-humiliation?p=1055720#post1055720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I would probably require a sixth level elder power to allow a specific Discipline to work on Gafflings, a seventh level elder power to allow a specific Discipline to work on Jagglings, an eighth level elder power to allow a specific Discipline to work on Totem Avatars, and a ninth level elder power to allow a specific Discipline to work on Incarna (purchasing the higher level powers would not give you the capabilities of the lower level powers because they work on different spiritual 'frequencies'). While Obfuscate would work on anything trying to perceive you visually, you would need an Obfuscate 9 elder power to interfere with the spiritual perceptions of an Incarna. In the case of Dominate and Presence, you would have to be able to perceive a spirit to be able to benefit from using the elder powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I would more format it as a single power to affect spirits, and have successes determine the power level of spirits that could be effected. That tends to be more in line with how Disciplines are formatter I think.<br /> Slight nitpick. You have Totem Avatar and Incarna as separate. This is just my understanding but: Totems are Incarna. Totem Avatars (like pack spirits) are Jagglings (usually. Some really weak ones might be Gafflings). That being said, the power jumps between the tiers of spirits are significant. If I were to set it up the way you did (and the more I think about it, the more I like that setup), I think it would be more fitting to say:<br /> Level 6: Gafflings<br /> Level 8: Jagglings<br /> Level 10: Incarna<br /> <br /> Nothing below Antediluvians should be being compared to Incarna for sheer power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 02-27-2017, 03:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}